; The aegis_reader SELinux module (spec D6), rendered by aegis-podman. The containers that
; mount originals (gateway, operations, indexer and media) run as aegis_reader.process.
; The token in the block below becomes read-only rules (dir, file and lnk_file) for each
; root type the module covers; nothing here may grant a write.
;
; It inherits udica's base container template and its full network template, net_container,
; which gives the network access container_t normally has. The roles listen (the gateway on
; 8080 and 8081) and connect on ports that are not http_port_t (web on 8000, PostgreSQL);
; restricted_net_container allows name_connect to http_port_t only and no name_bind, so it
; would deny them. The host-setup script loads exactly the udica templates inherited here.
(block aegis_reader
    (blockinherit container)
    (blockinherit net_container)
    @@READ_RULES@@
)
